window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"sion","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Sion","Skill","Sion","Sion"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 4-5","text":"Charged Q plus E poke zone him clean off the farm — your first clear lead window."},{"when":"Locke level 6","text":"His Purgatory execute arrives, but your R engage threat answers it — play the even stage carefully."},{"when":"Your first item","text":"The zombie passive undoes his execute entirely — his best tool stops paying."},{"when":"Two-plus items","text":"HP-stacking and R engage overwhelm his single-target burst for good."}],"wants":{"you":["Q charges hidden behind minion timing","Passive shield banked before trades","HP stacked into an unexecutable wall"],"foe":["Your Q charge baited and interrupted","Kills confirmed before your zombie form","A burst target that stays killable late"]},"early":"Levels 1 through 3 are an even grind: your passive shield trades into his on-hits and everything hinges on Q charge timing rather than raw stats. The lane bends your way at 4-5, when the charged Q plus E poke combo starts zoning him off farm entirely — build your CS lead right there.","mid":"At 6 the lane briefly levels as your R engage answers Purgatory — it is 120s at rank 1, so the two minutes after he spends it belong to you. Grievous Wounds beats stacking armour here: Soul Ignition refunds part of the damage he takes and its damage is true. Keep stacking HP and let his window quietly expire.","late":"With items you overwhelm him outright: HP-stacking makes his single-target burst a rounding error and your R engage decides where fights happen. Charge Q from fog, run him over with the team behind you, and remember that even in death the zombie keeps swinging — he has no clean answer left.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your shield passive trades evenly against his on-hits.","At 2 neither side snowballs; it all hinges on your Q charge timing.","Level 3 stays even — your knockup spike has not landed yet.","At 4-5 charge Q the moment his 10s blink is spent and zone him off farm.","At 6 the lane briefly evens as your R answers his new engage-and-execute threat.","At first item your zombie passive undoes his execute — the stage tilts back to you.","With items your HP-stacking and R engage overwhelm his single-target burst."]});
